= Principal–agent problem — Simple =

A principal–agent problem appears when one person or organization asks another to act on its behalf but cannot perfectly observe what the agent knows or does. The two sides may also want different things. Contracts, monitoring, and incentives can reduce the problem but rarely erase it.

'''Important boundary:''' principal–agent problem ≠ employer–employee relationship only.

